# Netlify redirects. First match wins, so keep the more specific rules first.
#
# /m/* : short links for the printable QR cards generated by
#        embed-bourbon-trail-map.html. Two reasons these exist rather than
#        putting the full tracked URL in the QR:
#          1. A shorter payload means a lower QR version, which means chunkier
#             modules at the same printed size and a code that scans from
#             further away. ~144 chars was landing around version 9; these land
#             around version 4.
#          2. The URL is printed underneath the code as a fallback for anyone
#             who cannot scan, and 144 characters of UTM soup is unreadable and
#             untypeable.
#
# THESE ARE PERMANENT. The whole point is that a host prints a card once and it
# sits in a guest binder for years. Do not remove or rename /m/* paths. If the
# destination ever needs to change, change the right-hand side here and every
# card already in the wild keeps working. That flexibility is exactly why these
# are 302 and not 301: a 301 gets cached by browsers indefinitely and takes the
# ability to re-point them away from us.
#
# The tracking params live here rather than in the QR so the code stays short.
# utm_medium=qr is baked in because only the printed card uses these; the guest
# message and guidebook links are clicked rather than typed, so they carry their
# own full URLs with their own utm_medium and do not need shortening.

# Statewide uses the explicit slug "ky" rather than an empty region. Without it,
# a card with a property name but no region would produce /m/willow-creek-farmhouse
# and the first segment would be read as a region. map.html ignores a region it
# does not recognise, so region=ky simply shows everything.

/m/ky/:host        /map.html?utm_source=host&utm_medium=qr&utm_campaign=guest-map&utm_content=:host                  302
/m/ky              /map.html?utm_source=host&utm_medium=qr&utm_campaign=guest-map                                    302
/m/:region/:host   /map.html?region=:region&utm_source=host&utm_medium=qr&utm_campaign=guest-map&utm_content=:host   302
/m/:region         /map.html?region=:region&utm_source=host&utm_medium=qr&utm_campaign=guest-map                     302
/m                 /map.html?utm_source=host&utm_medium=qr&utm_campaign=guest-map                                    302
